NAME
    pwd — Print the current working directory, because sometimes you
    need to know where you actually are.

SYNOPSIS
    pwd

DESCRIPTION
    The pwd command displays the absolute path of the current working
    directory.

    It takes no arguments and simply tells you where you are in the
    filesystem.

USAGE
    > pwd            # Displays the current working directory.

FUN FACTS
    - pwd stands for "print working directory".
    - It is useful when you have completely lost track of where you are.
    - Unlike a GPS, pwd only works with filesystems.
    - Running pwd never tells you how you got there.

EXAMPLES
    > pwd
        /home/user

    > cd documents
    > pwd
        /home/user/documents

SEE ALSO
    help(1), cd(1), ls(1), man(1)

    Remember, when you're lost in the filesystem,
    pwd knows exactly where you are.

